/T (Kolalanooduva" is authored by the Kannada saint-poet Vyasaraja Teertha, one of the foremost composers of the Haridasa tradition of devotional music. It speaks of Lord Krishna playing his flute in the groves of Vrindavana, and the enchantment bordering on chaos, that his melody stirs among all who hear it - the gopis, the cattle, and the very forest itself pauses to listen.)
